<?xml version='1.0' encoding='UTF-8'?>
<knowl mode="exercise" xmlns="https://spatext.clontz.org" version="0.2">
    <content>
        <p>
Use the theorems of pi-Base to prove that a space with these properties
        </p>
        <list>
            <!-- {{#hypotheses}} -->
            <item><p>{{{phrase}}}</p></item>
            <!-- {{/hypotheses}} -->
        </list>
        <p>
must {{{conclusion_must}}}.
        </p>
    </content>
    <outtro>
        <p>
Searching pi-Base for <c>{{{search_query}}}</c> shows that this combination
is impossible, using {{theorem_count}} theorems. One valid argument: suppose
the space has the three given properties, but is {{{negated_conclusion}}}.
        </p>
        <list>
            <!-- {{#derived_steps}} -->
            <item><p>
By <url href="{{{theorem.url}}}">{{theorem.uid}}</url> ({{{theorem.statement}}}),
the space {{{conclusion}}}.
            </p></item>
            <!-- {{/derived_steps}} -->
            <!-- {{#final_step}} -->
            <item><p>
But <url href="{{{theorem.url}}}">{{theorem.uid}}</url> ({{{theorem.statement}}})
now gives a contradiction.
            </p></item>
            <!-- {{/final_step}} -->
        </list>
        <p>
So the space must {{{conclusion_must}}}.
        </p>
    </outtro>
</knowl>
